    "created_at": "2016-07-28T17:59:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-28T17:59:38Z",
    "body": "I think the confusion is due to two different attributes being referred to here, the _content_ attribute and the _IDL_ attribute. Is this better?\n\n> If the `value` content attribute is present, user agents must parse it as an integer, in order to determine the value of the IDL attribute. If the content attribute's value cannot be converted to a number, the IDL attribute must be treated as if the content attribute was absent. The content attribute has no default value.\n\nThis is consistent with language regarding [reflected IDL attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#reflect) treating missing content attributes as an empty string, which in this case would be an invalid integer.\n",
